+            // demonstrably worked, and it is a write. A GET that remains readable after a downgrade
+            // is not evidence that a removed write privilege is still honoured -- and read endpoints
+            // are the ones that repeat harmlessly all over a generated test, so allowing them here
+            // is what turns this oracle into a false-positive generator (§5.1, the guard).
+            if (source.auth is NoAuth
+                || !isAllowed(source)
+                || source.verb !in listOf(HttpVerb.PUT, HttpVerb.PATCH, HttpVerb.POST, HttpVerb.DELETE)
+                // the guarded action must not itself be the transition endpoint, otherwise
+                // "demote A, then demote B" reads as a violation
